# Backups. The convention here is <name>.pre-<what>-<date>, and ktcommit.sh commits
# with `git add -A`, so every backup taken during a session went into a public
# archive: on 2026-09-22 that included a 6.4MB duplicate of the EPUB written by the
# publisher's own deploy step. The deliberate archive/backups-20260922/ folder is
# already tracked and stays tracked; this only stops new ones from being swept in.
*.pre-*
*.pre-update

# The session handoff. It is a working log -- what the last session was in the
# middle of, which deploy went where, what to pick up next -- written for the
# next operator and not for a reader. It was tracked until 2026-09-23; the
# history is still in git. The file stays at this path because the /decipher
# skill and the project memory both point at it.
RESUME.md

# THE SITE'S ARTWORK AND THE ATLAS PLATES. None of this is evidence for the
# reading, and none of it was ever chosen for publication: ktcommit.sh ran
# `git add -A`, so every picture the site build left in the working tree was
# swept into a repository whose README says it holds everything needed to
# check the attempt. Five maps and a book rendered in 3D are not that. They
# stay on disk, the site build still reads them, and they regenerate --
# the plates from harness/atlas.json through harness/ktatlas.py, which are
# tracked, along with the gate that checks their facts have sources.
work/rohonc/atlas/
work/rohonc/glass/
work/rohonc/glass.png
work/rohonc/book3d.png
work/rohonc/spin-*.webp

# A stray before-copy that predates the rule in archive/README.md.
work/rohonc/translation/reading.md.raw-*

# The Voynich planning memo. Written before any code existed and superseded by
# RESULTS.md, which carries the numbers. Nothing reads it. It was the only file
# in the repository naming individual models, against the site's own standing
# rule to name Anthropic's Claude and no other, and the last place still saying
# the work was private. Kept on disk; it is not a deliverable.
notes/VOYNICH_PLAN.md

# Király and Tokai's whole dictionary entries joined to every folio, in their
# own words. A local working file made by harness/ktsenses.py --all from data/;
# it is their dictionary and is not part of this repository.
work/rohonc/senses.json

# Two more local working files made from Király and Tokai's material: the sign
# outlines (harness/ktsigns.py) and the every-sense reading (harness/kttranslate.py).
# The site and the checks read them on disk; both regenerate from data/.
work/rohonc/signs.json
work/rohonc/translation/rohonc_reading_full.txt
